The wands are very powerful. Even complete melee fighters need them for
ranged attacks. There are so many ways to do things. Evoke blink, rage,
invisibility.. so many tactics. In Nethack the combat is trivial, almost
no danger involved. In Crawl it's the meat of the game. 

What I admire about Crawl is that you simply DO everything - ID almost
everything by trying out and the guerilla battle tactics. The tiles
version is very well done too - I love simply clicking on the minimap
and travel to that spot. It may sound a bit funny but there's a great
deal of old-school game ethics in this particular roguelike. Back when
roguelikes were born everything had to be simple because of technical
limitations. Now I really like how they've taken this idea of simplicity
onward when other roguelikes get more and more lost in petty details and
stupid death traps.
I've had Crawl characters die of stupidity but YASDs are pretty rare.
Nothing like an honorable fighting death :)


